WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:26.980
One of the best achievements of our show is
the combination between what’s real and

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:31.840
what’s not. That’s what distinguishes
our show from a lot of things, because we

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.880
try not to separate from reality.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:45.680
If everything was special effects, we would
be on a set right now, instead of 
the meditarrean coast of Spain. We need this

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:55.590
on our skin, the sun, the old castles built
by the Moors. I have Spanish dust between

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:57.390
my fingers right now. You can’t get that
on a set.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:04.080
Spain is so massive. Its locations, its views.
We could do a kind of itinerant show this

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:08.380
year. We had so many new worlds to visit,
we went from the north side of Spain to the

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:10.660
south.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:18.349
We had five different locations in five different
cities. In the north, a little more green.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:20.380
In the south, a little more desert. The Dothraki
we had in Spain were great.

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:27.700
We started the trip in Girona. We were there
for two weeks, in the city centre. Because

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:28.840
Girona is a nice city, a really beautiful
city.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:33.689
Yeah, we went to Girona. It’s a beautiful
medieval city. A perfect setting for Game

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:34.440
of Thrones.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:43.360
From Girona we traveled west many kilometers
to Bardenas Reales, a desert and mountainous

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:52.140
In the show we see beautiful deserts. It was
very funny, incredible. The last scene was

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:58.180
From there we went to Castillo de Zafra, in
the middle of nowhere, in a place called the

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:01.980
Spanish Siberia, because it’s one of the
coldest places on Spain.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:11.700
The location was absolutely unreal. It looked
like a set. From that place you could see

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:17.540
these huge plains, like the ones in Africa.
It was the most incredible place that I could

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:24.940
From there we went to Peñíscola. It’s
an old coastal town. A rocky town located

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:31.300
in the middle of the Mediterranean Sea. After
Peñíscola, we moved here, the last place

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:36.260
of the five in which we will work. But it’s
not the last location, because we’re going

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:39.800
to film in Almería, where we are right now.
We

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:42.220
have another five different locations.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:48.380
I lost track of so many different locations.
But each sequence of GOT has a couple of very

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:56.920
stunning moments. And being here, on the outskirts
of Almería has been for me one of these shocking

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:02.280
It’s been good coming back here. I never
lose that thrill as an actor. I had it in

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:12.800
a lot of movies. But in this show the level
is exceptional. What the people built. The

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:16.400
passion with which they work. And we 
have very committed extras.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:22.900
Last year, the level of extras we had here
in Spain was amazing. This year happened again.

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:29.860
I never met more hard-working people, happy
about being there. They infect everyone on

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:34.840
set. It’s a display of happiness, trust
and security. It was a joy.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:41.560
The show being back to Spain is 
very important for this country. Given the
dimensions of GOT, everyone loves it, the

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:49.280
people worked very excited. Wherever you go,
that’s the way it is. And it’s a pleasure,

